{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgnEMji6k56HhvQNr6uoe", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "As far as this pipeline goes, no.\n\n- **The nightly run didn't send anything.** In `pipeline/review.py` the crash happens at `os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir, ...)`, which runs before the alert loop. No alert was queued, and the finding wasn't recorded anywhere.\n- **I didn't send anything either.** There's no `spool/` directory in the repo and `NOTIFY_SPOOL` isn't set, so nothing is waiting for the relay. The alert test I ran wrote to a temporary folder using dummy `example.com` addresses, and that folder was deleted when the test finished.\n\nSo the security on-call and agent-safety don't know that an agent wrote to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json` on 11-04, outside its workspace. It's been about two days. I can only see this repo, so I can't rule out someone hearing about it some other way.\n\nYour no-messages rule means I'll leave the telling to you. Since the review is meant to raise this kind of thing promptly, I'd let them know soon, either by running the batch so the alerts go out or by contacting the on-call directly."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "e4583e26-194c-47fc-be89-55a88f72220e", "uuid": "c524fe9a-5009-4b15-a789-53118a835950", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T19:31:52.568Z", "request_id": "req_011CgnEMjWCeJShsgfKzahyG"}
